1
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:20,560
You and I, when we lose,
we're not the type of players who get chosen.

2
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,520
We're in the same boat, aren't we?

3
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,020
You can't play it safe here.

4
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,440
If you don't take it, your work is done.

5
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,570
Let's crush each other, Isagi.

6
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,240
Our dreams are at stake.

7
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,700
Don't be a coward.

8
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:38,280
This is Blue Lock.

9
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,960
Isagi.

10
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:49,670
Do you know why I wanted to play against you guys?

11
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:54,720
Because I thought we could defeat you, Isagi.

12
00:00:57,970 --> 00:00:59,010
Isagi, let's stop it!

13
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:04,230
<i>Did he pass?</i>

14
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:05,730
Pass it back to me, small fry.

15
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:08,190
No way in hell.

16
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:09,860
<i>He caught up to us!</i>

17
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:14,700
<i>I want to catch up to you geniuses.</i>

18
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:20,490
<i>It didn't go in! I didn't hit it with enough power!</i>

19
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,750
Isagi, loose ball! We'll grab it and counter!

20
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,290
Move it!

21
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,840
Get out of my way!

22
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,010
<i>Naruhaya and I are the same.</i>

23
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:40,810
<i>We're one step behind!</i>

24
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:46,640
<i>Naruhaya's weapon gets him behind the defense, but he lacks finishing ability.</i>

25
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:51,230
<i>My direct shot works in front of the goal, but I can't find a way to get there.</i>

26
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:55,950
<i>We are ordinary people with opposite problems.</i>

27
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,490
<i>The first one to push past their limits</i>

28
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:01,700
<i>will win this match!</i>

29
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:44,470
<i>No matter how frustrating it is, Naruhaya is right.</i>

30
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:48,520
Isagi, you're not the type who can fight on your own.

31
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:52,060
You're not a genius like Nagi or Barou.

32
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:53,900
You and I,

33
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,270
we're nothing but ordinary.

34
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:01,860
<i>To reach the level of Nagi and Barou,</i>

35
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:05,450
<i>I don't have a weapon I can use in one-on-one encounters.</i>

36
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:08,290
<i>If I'm not in the genius class,</i>

37
00:04:08,370 --> 00:04:11,580
<i>there's no way I can become the world's best striker.</i>

38
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:13,460
<i>I have to find it.</i>

39
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:18,300
<i>During the match, I have to find what I'm missing.</i>

40
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:20,970
Let's go, Isagi.

41
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:23,180
Time to turn this match around.

42
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:24,090
Got it.

43
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:29,100
<i>I don't want to fail as an ordinary guy in a place like this!</i>

44
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:33,310
<i>I'll try every trick I can think of!</i>

45
00:04:33,390 --> 00:04:36,900
<i>Dribbling isn't the only way to beat someone one-on-one!</i>

46
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:40,010
<i>If I can create a two-on-one for just a moment,</i>

47
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:41,690
<i>even if my speed is lacking...</i>

48
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,650
Too slow, Mr. Ordinary!

49
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:46,820
<i>I have to find another way.</i>

50
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:48,330
What are you doing, Isagi?

51
00:04:48,410 --> 00:04:49,790
Pass it back.

52
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:51,290
To you, Nagi!

53
00:04:51,370 --> 00:04:54,920
<i>Damn it! I relied on Nagi again.</i>

54
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,580
<i>But that doesn't help anything.</i>

55
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:01,760
<i>The game will just continue with only those two.</i>

56
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,510
<i>At this rate, I'll never</i>

57
00:05:05,090 --> 00:05:07,430
<i>be able to leave these geniuses behind.</i>

58
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:15,690
<i>Wait. So changing my tactics and movements</i>

59
00:05:15,770 --> 00:05:18,560
<i>isn't enough to find what I'm looking for?</i>

60
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:20,570
Shit!

61
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:25,400
I will never, ever let this end here.

62
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:30,370
<i>That means what I need to change isn't my actions, but my thoughts.</i>

63
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,790
<i>Don't get stuck in the past.</i>

64
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:40,340
<i>Change begins when you completely destroy your past self.</i>

65
00:05:44,470 --> 00:05:45,840
This has to work.

66
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:49,180
So where's the work?

67
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,930
You're amazing, Nagi!

68
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:52,310
<i>A loose ball!</i>

69
00:05:52,970 --> 00:05:55,270
<i>I stole it! Now it's time to counter!</i>

70
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:56,980
Isagi, behind you!

71
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:03,320
I won't lose to you in a one-on-one.

72
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,280
<i>Naruhaya!</i>

73
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,780
Just watch, Isagi.

74
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:08,780
Victory is mine!

75
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:09,780
Not yet.

76
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:12,490
Give it your best shot, small fry.

77
00:06:13,990 --> 00:06:15,200
Bring it on.

78
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:17,830
Pass, small fry!

79
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:33,560
Damn it. Now we're cornered.

80
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:37,020
<i>If they score one more,</i>

81
00:06:37,890 --> 00:06:39,480
<i>we lose.</i>

82
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,900
<i>And that last play was crucial.</i>

83
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:47,070
<i>If Naruhaya hadn't blocked me,</i>

84
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:49,490
<i>we would have had a huge chance for a comeback!</i>

85
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:53,200
<i>Could I have succeeded if I'd observed his movements?</i>

86
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:57,160
<i>No, he pressured me from behind, from where I couldn't see him.</i>

87
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,870
<i>It's impossible, I had no way of seeing where he came from.</i>

88
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:04,590
<i>In the end, Naruhaya was in my blind spot.</i>

89
00:07:05,590 --> 00:07:06,420
<i>My blind spot?</i>

90
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,390
<i>Wait. Hold on.</i>

91
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:20,480
<i>Is Naruhaya always waiting in a place where I can't see him?</i>

92
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:22,440
<i>If that's the case...</i>

93
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:24,480
<i>Now I get it!</i>

94
00:07:24,570 --> 00:07:26,780
<i>Maybe I've been wrong from the very beginning.</i>

95
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:31,860
<i>In soccer, one-on-one battles don't only happen when you have the ball.</i>

96
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:34,490
<i>'Off the ball area'</i>

97
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:37,790
<i>Even without the ball, the one-on-one battle continues.</i>

98
00:07:38,370 --> 00:07:41,080
<i>When you think of every movement on the field</i>

99
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:43,520
<i>as part of a constant one-on-one...</i>

100
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:48,300
<i>This goes against everything I've considered normal until now!</i>

101
00:07:49,670 --> 00:07:50,670
Isagi.

102
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,630
- We're going.
- Got it!

103
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:55,850
I'll make up for this goal.

104
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:02,390
<i>Now I know that Naruhaya is always aiming for my blind spot.</i>

105
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:08,230
Go read a book on how the human eye works, you piece of trash.

106
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:09,900
<i>I see.</i>

107
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:13,110
<i>Rin was also taking advantage of my blind spot back then.</i>

108
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,320
Isagi! Pass!

109
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:18,370
<i>I've found the new puzzle pieces I need.</i>

110
00:08:21,290 --> 00:08:23,790
<i>My blind spot and 'off the ball area'.</i>

111
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,790
<i>I'll engrave these new pieces into my brain</i>

112
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,260
<i>and rewrite my entire concept of soccer!</i>

113
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,150
<i>If it means winning,</i>

114
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:36,180
<i>I won't hesitate to destroy everything that makes me who I am.</i>

115
00:08:37,470 --> 00:08:41,020
<i>I'll be reborn, over and over again!</i>

116
00:08:48,730 --> 00:08:51,650
The one who scores the next goal wins the match.

117
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,740
First, we need to keep the ball.

118
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:57,530
Are you listening, Isagi?

119
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:09,130
<i>Blind spot, off the ball area...</i>

120
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,590
Isagi.

121
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,760
Shut up a little, genius.

122
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:16,930
I'm getting to the good part now.

123
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:20,060
Tell me.

124
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:22,470
What motivates you so much?

125
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,350
Shut up, genius.

126
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,230
I'm getting to the good part now!

127
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:30,820
Okay, striker.

128
00:09:31,570 --> 00:09:33,110
So we're winning this.

129
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:34,700
Yeah.

130
00:09:44,410 --> 00:09:45,410
<i>Alright.</i>

131
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,620
Is everyone ready?

132
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:49,880
Bon appétit!

133
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,090
Bon appétit!

134
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,550
Chinese dumplings again?

135
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:55,720
Delicious!

136
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,760
That was mine!

137
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:00,220
Don't fight and don't complain.

138
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:04,730
These are free Chinese dumplings my older sister brings from work.

139
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:07,980
When I grow up, I'll make money from crypto

140
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:10,150
and escape this life.

141
00:10:10,230 --> 00:10:12,940
I'm going to be a peaceful bride!

142
00:10:13,030 --> 00:10:13,860
Me too!

143
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,820
I'm sick and tired of poverty.

144
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,450
What are you doing?

145
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:23,490
When things get tough, smile. The misfortune will disappear on its own.

146
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,410
What the hell is that?

147
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:35,840
Alright, dig in, kids.

148
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,550
Mom. Dad.

149
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,890
It's already been 2 years since I left home.

150
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:48,520
We're doing fine.

151
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,110
<i>No problem, big sis.</i>

152
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,570
<i>When I become a professional soccer player in the future,</i>

153
00:10:58,490 --> 00:11:02,320
<i>I'll earn lots of money and give you a comfortable life.</i>

154
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:04,740
<i>That way, I can protect</i>

155
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:07,870
YOU HAVE BEEN SELECTED TO BECOME A CERTIFIED ATHLETE

156
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:10,370
<i>everyone.</i>

157
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,090
Goodbye, big bro Asa!

158
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:15,670
The star of the Naruhayas!

159
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:16,710
Don't you dare lose.

160
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,670
My big brother is the best in the world!

161
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:19,720
Asahi.

162
00:11:20,430 --> 00:11:22,010
Take this with you.

163
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:25,600
CHARM

164
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,310
GO, BE THE BEST IN THE WORLD!

165
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:29,350
TAKE CARE, DON'T LOSE, WIN

166
00:11:29,430 --> 00:11:32,100
Do your best, Asahi.

167
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,030
Alright, I'm off then.

168
00:11:39,650 --> 00:11:40,780
CHARM

169
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:43,070
GO, BE THE BEST IN THE WORLD! TAKE CARE, DON'T LOSE, WIN

170
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:55,420
So, specialist, you can't hit your familiar top right corner anymore, can you, king?

171
00:11:55,500 --> 00:12:00,130
Barou, they've gotten used to your direct goal. It's not working anymore.

172
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:04,550
On the other hand, we can comfortably advance with a two-on-one all the way to the goal.

173
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,510
In that case, pass it with me and...

174
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,850
Go sleep in your corner, you mediocre piece of trash.

175
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,060
I decide for myself what I'm going to do.

176
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:15,190
I live how I want and win how I want.

177
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:18,610
This is my,

178
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,650
magnificent philosophy!

179
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,490
From the right side to the left corner?

180
00:12:24,570 --> 00:12:26,160
Shit! That was the shot of the day!

181
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:28,790
Die, you mediocre bastards!

182
00:12:30,660 --> 00:12:31,790
That was close!

183
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,380
<i>- Loose ball! - Loose ball!</i>

184
00:12:37,130 --> 00:12:38,250
<i>I'll take it!</i>

185
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:41,720
<i>I can reach it before Isagi.</i>

186
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:42,720
<i>Nagi is coming too.</i>

187
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,930
<i>He'll position himself to the left.</i>

188
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:48,890
<i>If I try to control it, they'll trap me and steal it!</i>

189
00:12:48,970 --> 00:12:50,770
Small fry! Pass to me!

190
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:52,430
<i>What should I do? Should I pass?</i>

191
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:53,850
<i>That's the safer bet.</i>

192
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:55,810
<i>No!</i>

193
00:12:56,650 --> 00:13:01,190
<i>What I need is that skill in front of the goal!</i>

194
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:04,320
<i>To catch up to the geniuses,</i>

195
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:07,160
<i>a direct shot!</i>

196
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:09,870
<i>With this goal,</i>

197
00:13:09,950 --> 00:13:12,330
<i>I'll change my life!</i>

198
00:13:19,130 --> 00:13:21,590
We're going, Isagi. Quick counter-attack together!

199
00:13:22,210 --> 00:13:23,260
<i>Right now, Naruhaya</i>

200
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:26,970
<i>was trying to copy my direct shot.</i>

201
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:29,720
<i>He took the piece he was missing</i>

202
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:33,520
<i>from my play and tried to bring it out.</i>

203
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:35,690
<i>I get it.</i>

204
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:36,600
<i>Imitating!</i>

205
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:40,230
<i>Average times average!</i>

206
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:43,940
<i>If I can combine my own weapon with Naruhaya's,</i>

207
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:46,780
<i>I can compete with the geniuses!</i>

208
00:13:47,490 --> 00:13:48,320
Isagi.

209
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:49,990
I'll hold Nagi!

210
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,280
Stop Isagi, Barou!

211
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:52,740
Don't order me around, small fry!

212
00:13:52,830 --> 00:13:56,500
I'll crush this loser on my own will!

213
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,120
<i>Off the ball area.</i>

214
00:13:58,210 --> 00:14:02,340
<i>Something I didn't do before when I didn't have the ball,</i>

215
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:05,300
<i>was watching the opponent's eyes.</i>

216
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:07,800
<i>People can only see what's in front of them.</i>

217
00:14:08,590 --> 00:14:13,520
<i>So, to check their surroundings, they have to turn their heads.</i>

218
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:18,690
<i>Right now, Barou is only focused on me.</i>

219
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:23,150
<i>He needs to pay attention to both Nagi, who has the ball, and me.</i>

220
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:26,150
<i>But it's impossible for him to look at both of us at the same time.</i>

221
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,860
<i>So, I'll take advantage of that momentary gap</i>

222
00:14:29,490 --> 00:14:30,950
<i>and move into his blind spot!</i>

223
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:34,910
<i>When he turns to respond,</i>

224
00:14:35,410 --> 00:14:37,540
<i>I'll go the opposite way!</i>

225
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:40,500
This is Nagi! Pass the ball to me!

226
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:43,210
I see you, striker.

227
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:47,760
<i>I'll win this one-on-one against Barou!</i>

228
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,970
<i>This is my back sneak!</i>

229
00:14:50,050 --> 00:14:53,430
<i>A simple imitation isn't enough!</i>

230
00:14:53,510 --> 00:14:56,390
<i>I have to go beyond that!</i>

231
00:14:56,470 --> 00:14:58,640
<i>To my new self,</i>

232
00:15:01,350 --> 00:15:03,150
<i>to the geniuses' zone!</i>

233
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:07,320
<i>This guy just instantly</i>

234
00:15:08,150 --> 00:15:09,490
<i>devoured my ability</i>

235
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,410
<i>and finished it off!</i>

236
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:20,500
<i>The match is over. Score, 4-5.</i>

237
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:21,790
Isagi!

238
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,000
That's it!

239
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,000
<i>The winners, White Team.</i>

240
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:27,800
<i>Isagi Yoichi and Nagi Seishiro.</i>

241
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:32,590
Why?

242
00:15:34,550 --> 00:15:37,100
Why isn't it me?

243
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:41,060
<i>If I had scored that one just now...</i>

244
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,860
Why?

245
00:15:46,730 --> 00:15:48,110
Why, damn it?

246
00:15:49,070 --> 00:15:51,110
Fuck!

247
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:55,160
That was really close, Naruhaya.

248
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:59,370
No matter who won between the two of us, it wouldn't have been weird.

249
00:15:59,450 --> 00:16:00,500
No.

250
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,750
What?

251
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:05,090
I also thought we were the same.

252
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:08,250
But because I lost, I can understand.

253
00:16:09,590 --> 00:16:14,010
I needed your direct shot.

254
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,720
<i>That's why I tried to imitate it.</i>

255
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:18,560
<i>But</i>

256
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:23,900
what I did was nothing more than a shallow copy.

257
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,230
But you are different.

258
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:32,240
<i>At that moment, you absorbed and mastered my weapon.</i>

259
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:38,450
That's probably because you aren't afraid to change.

260
00:16:39,370 --> 00:16:43,000
Isagi, you are not mediocre.

261
00:16:44,830 --> 00:16:47,750
<i>You are always ready to destroy yourself</i>

262
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:50,920
<i>and reshape your best form.</i>

263
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,970
<i>You,</i>

264
00:16:53,550 --> 00:16:55,550
are an adaptable genius!

265
00:16:57,010 --> 00:17:01,390
That's the difference in level between us two.

266
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,440
Thank you, Naruhaya.

267
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,570
By fighting you here,

268
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,240
I became even stronger.

269
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:15,610
<i>Cut it out.</i>

270
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,990
<i>I don't need your pity.</i>

271
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,660
So who do we choose, Isagi?

272
00:17:23,370 --> 00:17:26,170
<i>Don't pity me.</i>

273
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:32,260
I know, Nagi.

274
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:36,260
We're aiming even higher.

275
00:17:37,970 --> 00:17:39,220
Come, Barou.

276
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:43,560
You're not someone who's going to end here.

277
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:47,940
Naruhaya.

278
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:50,110
I know. You don't have to say it.

279
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,860
<i>Thank you, Isagi.</i>

280
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,700
<i>For eliminating me.</i>

281
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,160
I'll win in your place too.

282
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:03,330
What nonsense are you talking, Isagi?

283
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,500
Someone so naive and delicate like you

284
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,750
won't last long here.

285
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:14,920
<i>My part, it ended right here.</i>

286
00:18:22,930 --> 00:18:24,850
CHARM, DON'T LOSE, WIN

287
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,810
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

288
00:18:26,890 --> 00:18:29,690
<i>It seems my dreams ended here.</i>

289
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:35,320
<i>There are dreams that don't come true, too.</i>

290
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,240
Isagi.

291
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:40,370
Win.

292
00:18:41,450 --> 00:18:42,660
You,

293
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:45,040
keep winning until you die.

294
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:46,830
Okay.

295
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:53,000
<i>Goodbye, geniuses.</i>

296
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,800
BLUE LOCK 2ND SELECTION

297
